The anomaly is an engine cost-model defect, not a signal result: the engine adds slippage to the fill price on both buys and sells, so slippage is a gain on sells, and the constant-dollar sizing makes low-priced/high-turnover nulls generate enormous commissions and negative equity. I'll record this as a limitation, keep the predeclared classification, and fix the cross-consistency reference lookup.
